@startuml GITGLE High-Level System Overview
title GITGLE: High-Level System Architecture Overview

package "User Interface" {
  [CLI Interface]
}

package "GITGLE Search Engine" {
  package "Data Acquisition" {
    [Crawl Pipeline]
  }
  
  package "Data Processing" {
    [Index Pipeline]
  }
  
  package "Query Processing" {
    [Search Pipeline]
  }
}

package "Core Components" {
  package "Services" {
    [GitHub API Client]
    [Text Processing]
    [Ranking Engine]
  }
  
  package "Distributed System" {
    [MapReduce Engine]
    [Key-Value Store]
    [Node Communication]
  }
}

package "External Services" {
  [GitHub API]
}

[CLI Interface] --> [Crawl Pipeline]
[CLI Interface] --> [Index Pipeline]
[CLI Interface] --> [Search Pipeline]

[Crawl Pipeline] --> [GitHub API Client]
[Crawl Pipeline] --> [Key-Value Store]
[Crawl Pipeline] --> [MapReduce Engine]

[Index Pipeline] --> [Text Processing]
[Index Pipeline] --> [Ranking Engine]
[Index Pipeline] --> [Key-Value Store]
[Index Pipeline] --> [MapReduce Engine]

[Search Pipeline] --> [Text Processing]
[Search Pipeline] --> [Ranking Engine]
[Search Pipeline] --> [Key-Value Store]

[GitHub API Client] --> [GitHub API]

[MapReduce Engine] --> [Key-Value Store]
[MapReduce Engine] --> [Node Communication]

note bottom
  **Three Core Pipelines:**
  
  1. **Crawl**: Fetch GitHub repos via API
  2. **Index**: Build searchable inverted index
  3. **Search**: Execute queries and rank results
end note

@enduml
